Patch 34: stop zeroing 128 KB of palette map on every mode search.

Bit-exact. Standalone, against anchor 7368e76. Independent of patch 0035.

This is a rebuild of a patch that was measured and verified in August but never
landed; the branch carrying it was deleted, so it is re-derived and re-verified
here against the current tree, which is unchanged in this area.

THE FINDING. A callgrind profile of the current tip (320x192, 3 frames,
cpu-used=5) attributes 2.45% of retired instructions to libc memset reached
through av2_rd_pick_intra_sby_mode. The source is one line, at two call sites:

    av2/encoder/intra_mode_search.c:1781   av2_zero(x->winner_mode_stats);
    av2/encoder/rdopt.c:9626               av2_zero(x->winner_mode_stats);

and the sizes, measured on this tree:

    WinnerModeStats           66,240 bytes
      MB_MODE_INFO               632
      RD_STATS                    40
      color_index_map         65,536     <- MAX_SB_SQUARE, 256x256
    array of 2, zeroed       132,480 bytes per call

**98.9% of the 132 KB cleared on every mode search is the palette colour map.**
A 4x4 luma block's intra mode search zeroes 128 KB of palette reconstruction
state before it starts. Note the profile only catches the intra call site; the
inter one at rdopt.c:9626 fires far more often in a random-access encode.

WHY THE MAP DOES NOT NEED CLEARING. color_index_map is palette reconstruction
state. The palette search writes a winner's map at the moment it records that
winner, and nothing reads the map of a winner that was never recorded --
x->winner_mode_count bounds the valid entries and is reset to zero on the line
immediately after this call. The array is written before it is read.

WHAT THE PATCH DOES. Adds av2_reset_winner_mode_stats() in block.h, which
clears every field of WinnerModeStats except color_index_map, and calls it from
both sites. The fields are cleared one at a time rather than as a byte span, so
that adding a member to the struct produces a compile-time reminder rather than
a silently uninitialised field.

BIT-EXACTNESS, MEASURED on this tree. Four configurations, two clips, three
presets, two QPs -- every one byte-identical to the unpatched encoder:

    320x192 cpu-used=4 qp110   a271350b93a4a028 == a271350b93a4a028
    320x192 cpu-used=4 qp185   4073825a8e6d892f == 4073825a8e6d892f
    320x192 cpu-used=2 qp160   5713e61f499d46d2 == 5713e61f499d46d2
    640x360 cpu-used=5 qp160   d434144611e1e035 == d434144611e1e035

This is evidence, not proof: it shows the map is written before it is read on
these paths, not on all paths. A CTC run reporting 0.00% BD-rate on every
metric is the check to insist on -- which is exactly what a bit-exact patch
should return, and what the temporal-filter SSE2 patch did return.

ON MEASURING THE SPEEDUP. Do not use wall clock for this. On the machine it was
developed on the noise floor is several percent, far above what this change
produces, and two configurations disagreed in sign. Retired-instruction counts
under callgrind are deterministic to well under 0.1% and are the right
instrument. One caveat on reading them: the work removed is memory traffic, and
a vectorised memset retires few instructions per byte written, so instruction
counts probably UNDERSTATE the wall-time gain. Treat the figure as a floor.

WHAT TO RUN. One arm at any preset -- the change is preset-independent and the
question ("is it still 0.00% BD at CTC scale?") is the same everywhere. The
cheapest preset is the right place to ask it.

RELATED, NOT IN THIS PATCH. The same profile shows two more memory-traffic
lines, and together the four account for about 10% of retired instructions:

    4.28%  memset via av2_build_inter_predictors   (xd->mv_refined, 8 KB/call)
    2.45%  memset via av2_rd_pick_intra_sby_mode   (this patch)
    2.40%  memcpy via av2_rd_pick_intra_sbuv_mode  (MB_MODE_INFO struct copies)
    1.00%  avm_memset16 via av2_build_intra_predictors_high

The mv_refined one looks like an obvious bounded-clear candidate and is NOT.
av2_build_inter_predictors clears 2 * N_OF_OFFSETS entries; the caller
initialises only [0, 2*n_blocks) before calling av2_get_optflow_based_mv -- but
make_inter_pred_of_nxn (reconinter.c:1583) reads mv_refined[n_blocks*2 + ref],
one past that range, and reconinter.c:3741 indexes the array at a TIP-specific
offset. A bounded clear must cover both. That check has to be done before the
change is safe, so it is written down here rather than shipped half-verified.

diff --git a/av2/encoder/block.h b/av2/encoder/block.h
index a5adfb2..fe87a5b 100644
--- a/av2/encoder/block.h
+++ b/av2/encoder/block.h
@@ -1659,6 +1659,39 @@ static AVM_INLINE bool is_bsize_gt(BLOCK_SIZE bsize1, BLOCK_SIZE bsize2) {
          block_size_high[bsize1] > block_size_high[bsize2];
 }
 
+/*!\brief Reset the winner-mode bookkeeping without clearing the palette map.
+ *
+ * `av2_zero(x->winner_mode_stats)` clears 132,480 bytes, of which 131,072
+ * (98.9%) is the two `color_index_map[MAX_SB_SQUARE]` arrays. Those arrays are
+ * palette reconstruction state: the palette search writes a winner's map when
+ * it records that winner, and nothing reads the map of a winner that was never
+ * recorded (`x->winner_mode_count` bounds the valid entries and is reset to
+ * zero alongside this call).
+ *
+ * Zeroing them costs 128 KB of memory traffic per mode search, at both call
+ * sites, to initialise storage that is written before it is read.
+ *
+ * Every other field is still cleared, field by field rather than by a span, so
+ * that adding a member to WinnerModeStats produces a compile-time reminder
+ * rather than a silently uninitialised field.
+ */
+static INLINE void av2_reset_winner_mode_stats(MACROBLOCK *x) {
+  const int n =
+      (int)(sizeof(x->winner_mode_stats) / sizeof(x->winner_mode_stats[0]));
+  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
+    WinnerModeStats *const ws = &x->winner_mode_stats[i];
+    av2_zero(ws->mbmi);
+    av2_zero(ws->rd_cost);
+    ws->rd = 0;
+    ws->rate_y = 0;
+    ws->rate_uv = 0;
+    ws->mode = 0;
+    ws->refs[0] = 0;
+    ws->refs[1] = 0;
+    // ws->color_index_map is deliberately NOT cleared -- see above.
+  }
+}
+
 static INLINE void set_blk_skip(uint8_t txb_skip[], int blk_idx, int skip) {
   if (skip)
     txb_skip[blk_idx] |= 1UL;
